# CODEOWNERS — automatic review assignment for path-sensitive files.
#
# Format: <path-pattern> <@user-or-team> [<@user-or-team> ...]
#
# Compliance artifacts are registry-level contracts that the
# `build_analysis` composition node enforces at graph-execution time.
# A drift here is a SOX §404 issue (the production audit trail no
# longer reflects what the compliance team classified), not an
# engineering one — so changes REQUIRE a compliance-team reviewer on
# every PR.
#
# See: compliance/audit_bearing_registry.md (workshop minutes,
# 2026-04-22) and prompts/pre_code_session.md §"WORKING-STYLE
# CONSTRAINTS".

# Audit-bearing field registry (machine-readable + minutes).
# Both files must stay in sync; any change ships through compliance.
/compliance/                   @compliance-team
/compliance/**                 @compliance-team

# The terminal status vocabulary is tightly coupled to the registry
# — AUDIT_CONTEXT_MISSING is what the enforcement node emits on a
# missing audit-bearing field. Review alongside compliance whenever
# it changes.
/contracts/models.py           @compliance-team @backend-team

# The composition node + adapter registry are the code paths that
# consume the registry. Code review from both compliance and backend
# keeps the contract and implementation honest against each other.
/api/analysis_composer.py      @compliance-team @backend-team
/api/analysis_adapters.py      @backend-team
/api/schemas.py                @backend-team

# Policy constants (thresholds that the shadow + recipes read).
/contracts/policy.py           @compliance-team @backend-team

# Pre-session prompt documents the working-style constraints and
# registry-first discipline; compliance should see changes to its
# section alongside platform.
/prompts/pre_code_session.md   @platform-team @compliance-team


# =====================================================================
# ADR-038 §8.5 — Five-layer CODEOWNERS map
# =====================================================================
#
# The case-centric architecture (ADR-038) introduces a five-layer
# stack: L0 Knowledge → L1 Deterministic primitives → L2 Bounded
# LLM primitives → L3 Case Agent → L4 Harness. Each layer carries
# distinct review requirements; this section makes them
# machine-enforced.
#
# See: architecture_v5.md §1 (layer responsibilities) and
# docs/adr/ADR-038-case-centric-order-intake.md §8.5.

# L0 — Knowledge layer. Skill bundles, compaction templates, the
# L2 LLM Shadow bundle, SLA policy. Compliance + domain SME hold
# veto on every change since these drive both reasoning surface
# and audit-bearing decisions.
/knowledge/                    @compliance-team @domain-sme @backend-team
/knowledge/**                  @compliance-team @domain-sme @backend-team
/knowledge/shadow_llm/         @compliance-team @backend-team @tools-admin
/knowledge/shadow_llm/**       @compliance-team @backend-team @tools-admin
/knowledge/compaction/         @compliance-team @backend-team
/knowledge/compaction/**       @compliance-team @backend-team
/knowledge/policy/             @compliance-team @backend-team
/knowledge/policy/**           @compliance-team @backend-team

# L1 — Deterministic primitives. Recipes, deterministic Compliance
# Shadow, gateway operations, validators. Backend leads; recipes
# also need compliance review when they touch authorisation logic.
/recipes/                      @backend-team
/recipes/**                    @backend-team
/compliance/shadow.py          @compliance-team @backend-team
/gateways/                     @backend-team
/gateways/**                   @backend-team
/constraints/                  @backend-team
/constraints/**                @backend-team

# L2 — Bounded LLM primitives. Constrained-output single-call LLM
# primitives (intent classifier, recipe selector, attachment
# extractor, L2 LLM Shadow). Compliance + Tools Admin hold veto
# alongside engineering — these calls feed verdicts capable of
# escalating cases (L2 LLM Shadow) or extracting audit-bearing
# fields from documents (extract_attachment).
/compliance/shadow_llm.py            @compliance-team @backend-team @tools-admin
/compliance/shadow_llm_azure.py      @compliance-team @backend-team @tools-admin
/agents/primitives/                  @backend-team @tools-admin
/agents/primitives/**                @backend-team @tools-admin
/agents/primitives/extract_providers.py  @compliance-team @backend-team @tools-admin
/constraints/llm_backend.py          @backend-team @tools-admin
/constraints/router.py               @backend-team @tools-admin

# L3 — Case Agent. The bounded while-loop, working-memory loader,
# tool registry, budget enforcer. Engineering + Compliance veto
# (the agent's tool-call sequence is the audit replay subject).
/agents/case_agent.py          @compliance-team @backend-team
/agents/case_tools.py          @compliance-team @backend-team
/agents/working_memory.py      @backend-team
/agents/budget.py              @backend-team

# L4 — Harness. Cross-cutting concerns: per-case mutex, tool-call
# interception, tier graduation, compaction trigger, L2 Shadow
# invocation, SLA monitor. Engineering + SRE hold review (the
# harness owns operational invariants like the cross-pod lock).
/agents/harness.py             @backend-team @sre-team
/agents/compaction.py          @backend-team @compliance-team
/agents/sla.py                 @backend-team @compliance-team
/agents/backfill.py            @backend-team @sre-team

# Orchestration node integration of L2 Shadow + case-agent dispatch
# is load-bearing for both Compliance (verdict authority) and SRE
# (graph traversal). Pin both reviewers.
/orchestration/nodes.py        @compliance-team @backend-team
/orchestration/graph.py        @backend-team

# Database migrations affect persistence shape — DBA + backend.
/db/migrations/                @backend-team @sre-team
/db/migrations/**              @backend-team @sre-team
/db/repository.py              @backend-team

# k8s manifests — SRE owns deployment surface.
/k8s/                          @sre-team
/k8s/**                        @sre-team
/Dockerfile.*                  @sre-team @backend-team

# Architecture spec + ADRs — Architect + Compliance review every
# change. Workshops produce the pre-read; the doc capture goes
# through the same review.
/architecture_v*.md            @architect @compliance-team
/docs/adr/                     @architect @compliance-team
/docs/adr/**                   @architect @compliance-team
/docs/workshops/               @architect @compliance-team
/docs/workshops/**             @architect @compliance-team
/docs/runbooks/                @sre-team @architect
/docs/runbooks/**              @sre-team @architect

# tasks.md — the single source of truth for project state. Every
# tick or new bullet should be visible to both compliance + backend.
/tasks.md                      @compliance-team @backend-team @architect
